   "RaceName": "State Representative Pos. 1",
   "Statement": "<b>Elected Experience</b><br/><br/><span></span>\r\n<p><span>State Representative, 28th LD; Co-Chair, Joint Military and Veterans Affairs Committee; Member, Postsecondary Education and Workforce Committee, Appropriations, Capital Budget, Rules, and WA Task Force Against Trafficking of Persons.</span></p>\r\n<span><br />\r\n</span><br/><br/><b>Other Professional Experience</b><br/><br/><span>Family small business owner; longtime administrator, Pierce and Tacoma Community Colleges; former Deputy Director, Pierce County&rsquo;s human services.</span><br/><br/><b>Education</b><br/><br/><span></span>\r\n<p><span>PhD, Oregon State University; M.Ed. and B.A., Western Washington University; A.A.S., Tacoma Community College.</span></p>\r\n<span><br />\r\n</span><br/><br/><b>Community Service</b><br/><br/><span>Former PTSA leader; YMCA Board Member; Past Chair, Pierce County Ethics Commission; NCSL Co-Chair Military and Veterans Affairs and Labor and Economic Development Committees; married, mother of seven, including two adopted from foster care.</span><br/><br/><b>Statement</b><br/><br/><span></span>\r\n<p><span>I&rsquo;m proud of my bipartisan record delivering for local families and businesses. Committed to safe communities, I worked with law enforcement to secure resources and tools to keep us safe. To address the affordable housing crisis, I supported emergency housing and affordability for seniors, working people, and military families. In education, I&rsquo;ve invested in affordable childcare, training, and improved K-12 outcomes.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p><span>I&rsquo;m a military mom and daughter, recognized as a leader in protecting those who serve and sacrifice. A longtime champion for workforce education, I&rsquo;m focused on local jobs and opportunity. Let&rsquo;s keep working together for the future we deserve.</span></p>\r\n<br /><br/><br/>",
