   "Statement": "<b>Elected Experience</b><br/><br/><p>Board member, ARNP&rsquo;s United</p><br/><br/><b>Other Professional Experience</b><br/><br/><p>20-year Army Officer/combat veteran, nurse practitioner, Associate\r\nDean, tenured educator, healthcare leader, and small business owner.&nbsp;</p><br/><br/><b>Education</b><br/><br/><p>Doctorate, Marymount University; Masters, Pacific Lutheran\r\nUniversity; Bachelors, Eastern Washington University; Associates, Spokane Falls\r\nCommunity College. Board-certified Family and Emergency Nurse Practitioner.&nbsp; Fellow: American Academy of Nursing, Academy of\r\nEmergency Nursing, and Academy of Wilderness Medicine.</p><br/><br/><b>Community Service</b><br/><br/><p>Provides free sports physicals, mentors nurse practitioner\r\nstudents in community-based care, precepts students from regional universities.&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Performs military readiness exams. Active in healthcare\r\neducation, workforce development, patient advocacy, and professional mentorship\r\nthrough teaching, guest lecturing, and leadership service in state and national\r\nhealthcare organizations.</span></p><br/><br/><b>Statement</b><br/><br/><p>I&rsquo;ve spent my life serving patients, students, military\r\nfamilies, and this community. I&rsquo;ve seen the real-world consequences when\r\ngovernment loses focus on the people it serves.&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Families are struggling with rising costs, housing\r\naffordability, public safety concerns, and declining trust in government. Small\r\nbusinesses and working families deserve leadership that listens, understands\r\ntheir challenges, and delivers practical solutions.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">I&rsquo;m running to bring accountable, service-driven leadership\r\nto Olympia &mdash; focused on people, results, and restoring trust between government\r\nand the communities it serves, not partisan politics or political theater.</span></p><br/><br/>",
